{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>A second time.</b> A second occurrence." "<b>The affliction has darkened.</b> Many of the sages said it is like וְתִכְהֶין עֵינָיו מֵרְאוֹת (and his eyes are darkened from seeing), and they said that the meaning of darkened white patches is like a reddish-white, that both are present in it. In my opinion, the word כהה is the opposite of פשה (spread), derived from וְתִכְהֶין עֵינָיו and its near-neighbor וְלֹא כָהָה בָּם. And the sense of לֹא פָשָׂה הַנֶּגַע is in another place. And behold, these are two signs: that the afflicted spot has darkened and has not spread — it is clean." "<b>And he shall pronounce him clean.</b> He declares that he is clean, for it was a scaly eruption; and if it spread afterward, it is impure."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:49.915339555Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}